<title>ALGERIA: Algerian research company makes $1.8 mln loss.</title>
<headline>Algerian research company makes $1.8 mln loss.</headline>
<dateline>ALGIERS 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>An Algerian research company, ENDMC, made a loss of 103.2 million dinars ($1.8 million) in 1995, the official Algerian news agency APS said on Monday.</p>
<p>It gave no comparative figures but said the National Enterprise for Industrial Development and Research of Construction Materials had a turnover in the year of 447.6 million dinars. The company has a capital of 50 million dinars.</p>
<p>($1 =55 dinars)</p>
</text>
